  The 7 Concepts You Should Learn In Depth
  
  1. Embeddings — What They Are and Why They Matter
  
  Where in code: EmbeddingConfig.embeddingModel() and every call to embeddingModel.embed(text)
  
  An embedding is a vector (array of floats) that represents the meaning of text. The key insight: texts with similar meanings produce vectors that are
  close together in vector space.
  
  // From LogIngestionService.ingest():
  Embedding embedding = embeddingModel.embed(segment.text()).content();
  // This converts "ERROR db Connection timeout" → float[384]
  // (AllMiniLmL6V2 produces 384-dimensional vectors)
  
  Why this matters for log analysis: the question "What database errors occurred?" and the log line "ERROR db Connection timeout" have similar embeddings
   even though they share almost no exact words. This is semantic search — matching by meaning, not keywords.
  
  Learn more:
  
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#embedding (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#embedding) — LangChain4j embedding concepts
  - https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/embeddings (https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/embeddings) — OpenAI's explanation of embeddings
  (conceptual, applies to any model)
  - https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2) — The actual model used
  in your project
  
