  2. The AllMiniLmL6V2 In-Process Embedding Model
  
  Where in code: EmbeddingConfig.java
  
  @Bean
  public EmbeddingModel embeddingModel() {
      return new AllMiniLmL6V2EmbeddingModel();
  }
  
  This is a sentence-transformer model that runs entirely inside your JVM via ONNX Runtime. Key properties:
  
  - 384 dimensions — each text becomes a float[384]
  - No API key needed — unlike OpenAI's text-embedding-ada-002
  - Fast — runs locally, no network latency
  - Trade-off — less powerful than OpenAI's embedding models, but perfect for learning and many production use cases
  
  The Maven dependency langchain4j-embeddings-all-minilm-l6-v2 bundles the ONNX model file inside the JAR. When you call new AllMiniLmL6V2EmbeddingModel(),
  it loads the model into memory once.
  
  Learn more:
  
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-models/in-process (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-models/in-process) —
  LangChain4j in-process embedding models
  - https://onnxruntime.ai/ (https://onnxruntime.ai/) — ONNX Runtime (the engine that runs the model in Java)
  
