  3. Vector Store (EmbeddingStore) and Similarity Search
  
  Where in code: EmbeddingConfig.embeddingStore() and RagService.retrieve()
  
  @Bean
  public EmbeddingStore<TextSegment> embeddingStore() {
      return new InMemoryEmbeddingStore<>();
  }
  
  The EmbeddingStore is a vector database — it stores embeddings alongside their original text (TextSegment) and supports similarity search. The
  InMemoryEmbeddingStore keeps everything in a List in memory.
  
  The critical operation is findRelevant:
  
  // From RagService.retrieve():
  Embedding questionEmbedding = embeddingModel.embed(question).content();
  return embeddingStore.findRelevant(questionEmbedding, MAX_RESULTS, MIN_SCORE);
  //                                  ↑ query vector    ↑ top-K     ↑ minimum cosine similarity
  
  What happens under the hood:
  
  1. The question is embedded into a vector
  2. findRelevant computes cosine similarity between the question vector and every stored vector
  3. Returns the top 5 (MAX_RESULTS) matches with similarity ≥ 0.5 (MIN_SCORE)
  4. Each EmbeddingMatch contains the score, the embedding, and the original TextSegment
  
  Cosine similarity ranges from -1 to 1 (for normalized vectors, 0 to 1). A score of 0.9 means "very similar meaning"; 0.5 is the threshold your code uses
  to filter out irrelevant results.
  
  Learn more:
  
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#embedding-store (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#embedding-store) — LangChain4j EmbeddingStore
  concepts
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-stores/in-memory (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-stores/in-memory) —
  InMemoryEmbeddingStore docs
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-stores/ (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/integrations/embedding-stores/) — All supported vector stores
