  4. TextSegment — The Unit of Storage
  
  Where in code: LogIngestionService.ingest()
  
  TextSegment segment = TextSegment.from(chunk);
  Embedding embedding = embeddingModel.embed(segment.text()).content();
  embeddingStore.add(embedding, segment);
  
  TextSegment is LangChain4j's wrapper for a piece of text that you want to store and retrieve. It can also carry metadata (key-value pairs) — your code
  doesn't use metadata yet, but in production you'd add things like:
  
  TextSegment segment = TextSegment.from(chunk, Metadata.from("source", "app.log")
                                                         .add("timestamp", "2026-04-25"));
  
  This lets you filter search results by metadata later (e.g., "only search logs from yesterday").
  
  Learn more:
  
  - https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#document-and-textsegment (https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/rag#document-and-textsegment) — TextSegment
  and Document concepts
  
